      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "According to HACCP guidelines, cooked poultry should be cooled to a temperature of 70°F (21°C) within 2 hours of cooking, or to 40°F (4°C) or below within 4 hours. Additionally, the cooling time is calculated from the finished cooking time of the product, so you should check your kitchen's specific schedules for accuracy. This will help prevent the growth of Clostridium perfringens and other pathogens.",
